  "summary": "A silencer reduces noise from gas flow (engine exhausts, blow-offs, vents). Reactive chambers and baffles reflect low-frequency sound back toward the source; absorptive packing behind a perforated tube converts high-frequency sound into heat. Combined designs cover a wide frequency range with low pressure drop.",
